    "created_at": "2026-06-13T00:57:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-13T00:57:51Z",
    "body": "I don't feel strongly about this either way. I can say that I don't remember any issue ever having been raised against the HTML checker for it. But if course that doesn't prove we've not had a lot of people being annoyed by it but just not reporting it. \n\nI vaguely remember when we originally added this (a long long time ago) but I don't remember why. I can imagine it was just under an assumption it was more likely to be the result of somebody doing a copy-paste or initially populate a list, but then forgetting to fill in one of the initial copy-pasted items with their actually-intended text. \n\nRegardless, I wouldn't object to the requirement being dropped.",
